Table~\ref{tab:main-results} establishes the headline comparison against the
full published benchmark. On the three datasets with matched preprocessing and
splits, the Anchor family attains the best value in all six dataset--metric
columns: \method{} is best or tied for best in five and second in the remaining
HumanActivity MAE column, where ERMAnchor is best. Within the separate MIMIC
Anchor evaluation, ERMAnchor has the lowest MSE and \method{} the lowest MAE, but
we do not interpret these values as a direct neural comparison. The matched
results motivate treating strong deterministic anchors as required controls.

