\section{Ablations}

\subsection{Candidate-removal ablations}

Table~\ref{tab:candidate-removal} removes candidate families from \method{}.
The ablation does not show that every component is universally necessary;
instead, it shows that the relevant mechanism is dataset dependent. EMA removal
hurts P12 and HumanActivity, sparse-history removal hurts USHCN, and phase
removal is especially damaging on USHCN. On P12 and MIMIC, ERM-style selection
already explains most of the gain, while the structural rules are decisive on
USHCN and match the full method on HumanActivity.

